  "nl_text": "The database schema, rschema_0255, is used to store data related to a production facility. It consists of 11 tables, each representing a different entity or aspect of the production process.\nThe first table, production_report, stores information about production reports, including the report ID, report type, date, production data, production indicators, completion status, metal recovery rate, and grade. The primary key is the report ID.\nThe second table, equipment, stores information about the equipment used in the production process, including the equipment ID, equipment name, model, main category, subcategory, location, and operation status. The primary key is the equipment ID.\nThe third table, equipment_inspection, stores information about equipment inspections, including the equipment ID, inspector ID, inspection plan, execution progress, and any related foreign keys. The primary key is the equipment ID and inspector ID, and there are foreign key constraints on the inspector ID and equipment ID referencing the user and equipment tables.\nThe fourth table, equipment_failure_reporting, stores information about equipment failures, including the equipment ID, failure reporter ID, failure type, failure time, and processing status. The primary key is the equipment ID and failure reporter ID, and there are foreign key constraints on the failure reporter ID and equipment ID referencing the user and equipment tables.\nThe fifth table, equipment_repair, stores information about equipment repairs, including the equipment ID, repair person ID, repair progress, repair time, and any related foreign keys. The primary key is the repair ID, and there are foreign key constraints on the repair person ID and equipment ID referencing the user and equipment tables.\nThe sixth table, quality_report, stores information about quality reports, including the report ID, metal recovery rate, warehouse sample, metal grade, recovery rate daily report, grade daily report, and any related foreign keys. The primary key is the report ID.\nThe seventh table, equipment_monitoring, stores information about equipment monitoring, including the equipment ID, equipment type, collected data, status, monitoring data, fault alarm, data visualization, and administrator ID. The primary key is the equipment ID and administrator ID, and there are foreign key constraints on the administrator ID and equipment ID referencing the user and equipment tables.\nThe eighth table, user, stores information about users, including the user ID, username, role, permissions, status, and operation history. The primary key is the user ID.\nThe ninth table, announcement, stores information about announcements, including the announcement ID, announcement content, release time, publisher ID, and announcement status. The primary key is the announcement ID, and there is a foreign key constraint on the publisher ID referencing the user table.\nThe tenth table, job_position, stores information about job positions, including the job ID, job name, job description, job responsibilities, and job requirements. The primary key is the job ID.\nThe eleventh table, user_job_application, stores information about user job applications, including the user ID, job ID, job match rate, and any related foreign keys. The primary key is the job ID and user ID, and there are foreign key constraints on the job ID and user ID referencing the job position and user tables.\nOverall, the schema is designed to store and manage data related to a production facility, including production reports, equipment, inspections, failures, repairs, quality reports, monitoring, users, announcements, job positions, and job applications. The schema is well-structured and organized, with clear primary and foreign key constraints, and appropriate data types for each column.",
  "gold_question": "Business Requirement Description :\n1.Production Statistics:\nProduction reports, displaying production data for each process. Information to be recorded includes the report type, date, production data, production indicators, completion status, metal recovery rate, and grade.\n2.Equipment Management:\nEquipment record management, including basic information (name, model, main category, subcategory, location, etc.). Equipment operation status, with real-time monitoring and alarm notifications in case of anomalies.\nEquipment inspection management, recording inspection plans and progress, performed by the inspector.\nEquipment failure reporting, recording information about the failure, including the reporter’s ID, failure type, failure time, and processing status.\nEquipment repair management, handled by repair personnel, recording repair details and progress, and managing repair work orders. Information such as repair progress and repair time should be recorded.\n3.Quality Management:\nQuality report module, displaying the recovery rate and grade for each metal. Records to include metal recovery rate, incoming warehouse sample, metal grade, recovery rate daily report, and grade daily report.\n4.User Management:\nFor each user in the system, the following details should be recorded: user ID, username, role, permissions, status, and operation history.\n5.Announcements:\nAnnouncers can create, publish, delete, and retrieve announcements. Information to record includes announcement content, release time, and announcement status.\n6.Job Positions:\nThe system should register currently available job positions, including position ID, position name, position description, position responsibilities, and job requirements. Users can apply for positions, and the system will record the position match rate.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0255.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0255\nCREATE TABLE `production_report` (\n  `report_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `report_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `report_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `production_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `production_indicators` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `completion_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `metal_recovery_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `grade` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`report_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment` (\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `equipment_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `model` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `main_category` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `subcategory` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `operation_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`equipment_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment_inspection` (\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `inspector_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `inspection_plan` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `execution_progress` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`equipment_id`, `inspector_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_inspection_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`inspector_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_inspection_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`equipment_id`) REFERENCES `equipment` (`equipment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment_failure_reporting` (\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `failure_reporter_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `failure_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `failure_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `processing_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`equipment_id`, `failure_reporter_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_failure_reporting_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`failure_reporter_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_failure_reporting_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`equipment_id`) REFERENCES `equipment` (`equipment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment_repair` (\n  `repair_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `repair_person_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `repair_progress` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `repair_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`repair_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_repair_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`repair_person_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_repair_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`equipment_id`) REFERENCES `equipment` (`equipment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `quality_report` (\n  `report_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `metal_recovery_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `warehouse_sample` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `metal_grade` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `recovery_rate_daily_report` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `grade_daily_report` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`report_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `equipment_monitoring` (\n  `equipment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `equipment_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `collected_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `monitoring_data` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `fault_alarm` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `data_visualization` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`equipment_id`, `administrator_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_monitoring_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`administrator_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `equipment_monitoring_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`equipment_id`) REFERENCES `equipment` (`equipment_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `permissions` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `operation_history` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `announcement` (\n  `announcement_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `announcement_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `release_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `publisher_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `announcement_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`announcement_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `announcement_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`publisher_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `job_position` (\n  `job_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `job_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `job_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_responsibilities` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_requirements` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`job_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user_job_application` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `job_match_rate` decimal(5,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`, `job_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `user_job_application_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `user` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `user_job_application_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`job_id`) REFERENCES `job_position` (`job_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
